    <summary>250+ tools for PDFs, images, text, SEO and everyday calculations, in one desktop app.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
ToolsMonk is a Windows desktop app that puts a large, practical toolbox in one window: PDFs, images, text, SEO checks and everyday calculations.

**Where your files are processed**

Most tools run entirely on your device. You pick a file, it is processed locally, and it never leaves your computer. A smaller number genuinely need a server, such as the AI features and the tools that fetch a page from the web. The app says which is which on the tool itself, and the full list is published at https://toolsmonk.com/where-your-files-are-processed

**What is inside**

* PDF: edit, merge, split, compress, rotate, crop, organise pages, add page numbers, watermark, sign, redact, unlock, repair, fill forms, and convert to and from Word, Excel, PowerPoint, images and plain text.
* Images: resize, crop, compress, convert between formats, remove backgrounds, upscale, batch process, and a layered photo editor.
* Text and developer: word and character counts, case conversion, formatting, comparison, JSON and CSV handling, hashing and encoding.
* Calculators: percentages, currency, dates, finance, health and study tools.
* SEO: site audits, meta and schema checks, speed tests, sitemap and robots tools.

**Notes**

* The upstream installer is not code signed. Chocolatey verifies the download with a SHA256 checksum instead.
* This package installs machine-wide (`/allusers`). The same installer run by hand installs per-user by default.

Documentation: https://sourceforge.net/p/toolsmonk/wiki/Home/
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/vksingh5995/toolsmonk-releases/releases/tag/v1.1.12</releaseNotes>
